# Walkthrough - Contact Page and Global Style Updates

I have successfully updated the SIPRAC website with a brand-new contact page and enhanced the home page with modern UI features and the requested color scheme.

## Global Styles and Layout
- **Off-white Background**: Set all pages to use a premium `#FAF9F6` background.
- **Sticky Header**: Implemented a modern navigation bar that hides on scroll down and reappears on scroll up.
- **Black Footer**: Created a comprehensive black footer with all the necessary contact information and links.
- **Typography**: Updated typography to use Montserrat for a professional, bold look.

## Contact Page
- **Hero Section**: Clean title and subtitle matching the reference.
- **Contact Info**: A grid of cards for Phones, Email, WhatsApp, and Opening Hours, each with its corresponding icon and orange branding.
- **Contact Form**: A professional form with icons, validation, and data protection checkboxes.
- **Location & Coverage**: Integrated a section detailing the coverage area in Colombia with a map placeholder.
- **FAQ**: Added an accordion for frequently asked questions.

## Home Page Enhancements
- **Infinite Carousel**: The "Nuestros Servicios" section now features a smooth, infinite horizontal scroll.
- **Liquid Glass Effect**: The "Beneficios" section cards now have a premium "liquid glass" hover effect.
- **Professional Clients Section**: Replaced the basic circles with a sleek, centered slider for client names.
- **Connected CTA**: All "Solicitar Asesoría" and "Consultoría" buttons are now correctly linked to the contact page.

## Verification
- Verified responsive design across all new sections.
- Ensured color consistency between orange, black, and white elements.
- Tested the sticky header behavior.
